  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in your account ACC-1005. The amount is **EUR 240.00**, a card payment to **TechMart Online** on 2026-07-20. The status is settled.\n\nYour records also show TX-0402: another EUR 240.00 card payment to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14. I'm noting it only because the two match in amount and merchant. I haven't assumed anything from it.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes I can open a dispute under, and what each one covers:\n\n- **duplicate_charge**: the same purchase was charged more than once. This could fit if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are two charges for one purchase.\n- **unauthorized_debit**: you did not authorise the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present**: a card payment was made without your card being present, and you did not make it. This is typically used for online fraud.\n- **goods_not_received**: you paid, but the goods were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered**: you paid, but the service was never provided.\n\nTell me what happened and I can check whether a dispute is eligible under the matching code before anything is filed. I won't open a dispute without your confirmation.",
